@startuml seq-create
!include style.iuml

title Create a task from the client (PUT on an unknown resource)

autonumber "<b>00"
participant "CalDAV client" as C
participant "PutHandler" as PH
participant "VTodoMapper" as VM
participant "DonetickApiClient" as API
participant "Donetick" as DT
participant "ChoreCache" as CC
participant "CalendarResolver" as CR

C -> PH : PUT /caldav/calendars/{user}/{slug}/{client-uuid}.ics\nBEGIN:VTODO UID:{client-uuid} SUMMARY:... DUE:...
PH -> PH : size guard (<= 1 MB), else 413
PH -> PH : parse with Ical.Net, else 400
PH -> PH : ResolveChoreId(path, UID)\n1. donetick-{id}.ics in path\n2. UID donetick-{id}@donetick\n3. UID map lookup
note right of PH : none matches, so this is a new task
PH -> PH : STATUS is COMPLETED?
note right of PH : no, so continue with create
PH -> VM : ToChoreLiteRequest(vtodo)
VM --> PH : {name, description?, dueDate? (yyyy-MM-dd)}
PH -> API : CreateChoreAsync(request)
API -> DT : POST /eapi/v1/chore
DT --> API : 200 DonetickChore {id: 42, ...}
API --> PH : created
PH -> CC : UpsertChore(created)  (new ETag, new CTag)
PH -> CC : MapUid(client-uuid, 42)
PH -> CR : GetSlugForChore(created)
note right of CR
  New chores have no labels via the eAPI,
  so the slug is always "tasks".
end note
PH --> C : 201 Created\nLocation: /caldav/calendars/{user}/tasks/donetick-42.ics\nETag: "..."

== Follow-up within the same process lifetime ==
C -> PH : PUT .../{client-uuid}.ics (edit before the client switched to the canonical URL)
PH -> CC : GetIdByUid(client-uuid)
CC --> PH : 42
PH -> PH : continue as update of chore 42

== Error handling ==
alt Donetick returns an error
  API --> PH : HttpRequestException
  PH --> C : 502 Bad Gateway
else Donetick returns an empty body
  PH --> C : 502 Bad Gateway
end
@enduml
